  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sustainable energy for good growth and development of Bangladesh</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nuvoton planned to invest in the development of a 5 ha PV-solar field for 3MWp in Bangladesh.Technical Assistance (DGGF-TA) was provided to conduct a Technical Feasibility Study with the aim to prepare for future investments through impact investors and possibly a DGGF loan and minimise technical risks of the provisioned investment.The study included the set-up of a local legal entity, developing a viable financial mode through a draft Power Purchase Agreement, assessing the technical feasibility of the solar field design, testing potential locations and local power distribution through mini-grids, location selection and a Social Environmental Impact Study (ESG compliant).The study demonstrated the feasibility of Mini Grid PV systems and resulted in partnerships with the local government for further development and investments in mini grid solar-fields which have the potential to provide at least 3,000 people in rural areas with access to sustainable energy sources and thus improving livelihoods.During the project, 20 direct jobs were supported and sustainable knowledge transfer was provided to 24 people.</narrative>
  </description>
